x86_64-linux  the recorded rule in docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol": every constructor and destructor here is written inside its class, so clang emits only the form a use asks for and cxx1 emits both of Itanium's - the extras are cxx1's C1 and D1 forms, and nothing clang wrote is missing or different. arm64-darwin agrees on all seventeen; what this case measures is the terminate row over the copy, which names.sh does not read and run.sh does.
